WEBVTT

00:15.439 --> 00:17.858
I can't believe you got a boyfriend.

00:17.941 --> 00:20.694
- Huh?
- What's wrong with that guy?

00:20.777 --> 00:23.655
He's delusional if he can't tell you're
a gorilla.

00:23.739 --> 00:24.781
What?!

00:25.741 --> 00:28.285
Sounds like maybe you're just jealous
of him.

00:28.368 --> 00:31.705
Keep it up and he's gonna see how weird
you are and dump you.

00:32.205 --> 00:35.917
Come and say that once you finally have
a successful relationship yourself.

00:36.001 --> 00:38.086
Although, I doubt you ever will.

00:40.714 --> 00:41.590
Shut up.

00:45.802 --> 00:46.720
Hey, don't worry!

00:48.055 --> 00:49.056
You piss me off!

00:49.765 --> 00:52.642
I THINK WE SHOULD BREAK UP

00:56.688 --> 00:57.689
I THINK WE SHOULD BREAK UP

00:57.773 --> 00:58.607
Why?

01:01.735 --> 01:02.694
Did I do something?

01:07.449 --> 01:10.535
He hasn't read my texts. What?
I'm blocked?

01:12.079 --> 01:13.830
It's all over!

01:16.708 --> 01:19.044
It's always over before it really begins.

01:19.920 --> 01:23.048
I wonder what he even liked about me
in the first place.

01:23.590 --> 01:24.966
He barely got to know me.

01:28.470 --> 01:31.765
Meanwhile, Koyun's been in a relationship
for so long.

01:31.848 --> 01:33.058
I'm kinda jealous.

01:35.227 --> 01:38.730
Tell me, Koyun, what is it you don't
like about Igarashi?

01:39.731 --> 01:40.565
Huh?

01:40.649 --> 01:43.652
I bet... there is a lot about him you can't
stand.

01:43.735 --> 01:44.569
AZUMI

01:44.653 --> 01:47.405
But he seems to really like you.

01:48.156 --> 01:51.034
Be glad someone likes you and stop
taking it for granted.

01:52.953 --> 01:53.912
Good point.

01:54.454 --> 01:57.332
I should be grateful that someone
even likes me.

01:58.625 --> 02:01.586
What if Igarashi's the only guy
out there...

02:02.087 --> 02:03.922
Who'll keep liking me.

02:04.714 --> 02:05.549
Koyun?

02:07.968 --> 02:09.302
So, where should we go next?

02:09.386 --> 02:10.303
Karaoke?

02:10.387 --> 02:11.763
Mmm, sure why not.

02:12.264 --> 02:15.100
- Could be fun.
- After that, Koyun dropped her club

02:15.183 --> 02:18.061
activities, and started dating Igarashi.

02:19.354 --> 02:22.315
I really wish I had never said
that to her.

02:23.400 --> 02:26.278
Be glad someone likes you and stop
taking it for granted.

02:27.154 --> 02:30.699
Does that mean this whole thing was my
fault?

03:56.368 --> 03:58.703
THE RAMPARTS OF ICE

04:02.874 --> 04:06.878
New Semester

04:09.089 --> 04:11.299
Ugh. This year's almost over.

04:11.800 --> 04:13.260
AMAMIYA RESIDENCE
LIVING ROOM

04:13.343 --> 04:15.971
He's probably sad the seniors are
graduating, right?

04:17.138 --> 04:18.473
No! That's not it!

04:18.556 --> 04:20.141
Why're you whining? Ah, the band girl?

04:20.225 --> 04:21.226
- THIRD YEAR
- Yup.

04:21.309 --> 04:23.019
I said that's not it!

04:23.520 --> 04:25.063
Just tell her how you feel.

04:25.146 --> 04:26.189
Sure.

04:26.273 --> 04:27.274
Yeah' well...

04:27.357 --> 04:30.277
You of all people will never understand
how I feel, alright?

04:30.360 --> 04:31.945
Hm, so you admit it, Hayato.

04:32.028 --> 04:33.530
I totally understand.

04:34.030 --> 04:35.240
Uh, no you don't!

04:35.865 --> 04:38.326
You've never been in love with anyone
before.

04:39.286 --> 04:40.578
Wow! That was rude.

04:41.079 --> 04:44.582
I'll have you know, I've always
liked people as much as they liked me.

04:44.666 --> 04:47.669
- That's exactly what I'm talking about!
- That's exactly what I'm talking about!

04:47.752 --> 04:49.546
That's just you not disliking anyone.

04:49.629 --> 04:51.006
Isn't that a good thing?

04:51.089 --> 04:52.340
I don't get why it's bad.

04:52.841 --> 04:53.883
It is bad.

04:53.967 --> 04:57.095
And that's why you don't freaking
react to getting dumped.

04:57.178 --> 05:00.849
Well, me getting depressed or not isn't
gonna change the fact they wanted

05:00.932 --> 05:02.642
to break up with me, y'know?

05:03.143 --> 05:04.269
Ugh...

05:04.352 --> 05:06.396
Drive me nuts, you know that?

05:06.896 --> 05:09.649
Someday, when you finally fall in love
with someone...

05:10.442 --> 05:13.945
And they don't care about you at all,
I hope it really pushes you over

05:14.029 --> 05:15.071
the deep end, man.

05:15.155 --> 05:16.031
Same!

05:16.114 --> 05:17.490
We're friends, right?

05:18.491 --> 05:20.201
See? Aren't they mean?

05:20.994 --> 05:21.828
Mm.

05:23.997 --> 05:26.499
Oh, I made her laugh.

05:27.834 --> 05:28.668
It's so cute.

05:28.752 --> 05:29.586
STARE

05:31.504 --> 05:32.964
AMAMIYA RESIDENCE
LIVING ROOM

05:33.048 --> 05:33.882
Ugh.

05:35.550 --> 05:37.677
I wouldn't do something so pointless
anyway.

05:37.761 --> 05:39.262
- I thought so.
- I thought so.

05:41.306 --> 05:42.432
Emotions...

05:43.683 --> 05:45.101
The more you show them...

05:45.185 --> 05:47.270
The more it puts you at a disadvantage.

05:51.066 --> 05:53.318
And it makes you more vulnerable.

05:58.782 --> 06:00.825
You know, I've always wondered.

06:01.826 --> 06:05.288
You tell me to set goals, but then you
stop me from chasing my dreams?!

06:05.372 --> 06:07.832
I can tell you're not being serious
about this.

06:08.333 --> 06:10.293
Anyway, aren't you just moving
out to mess around?

06:10.377 --> 06:11.378
I can't believe this!

06:11.461 --> 06:14.339
What the hell? You don't know what you're
talking about, you old bastard.

06:14.422 --> 06:15.256
Ah, they're so loud.

06:15.340 --> 06:18.259
He's nothing but a troublemaker.
Wish he'd leave already.

06:18.760 --> 06:21.012
People get emotional and argue.

06:21.971 --> 06:24.682
What feelings could make people go
that far?

06:26.518 --> 06:29.062
Emotions are just a product of your mind, right?

06:30.105 --> 06:32.190
So shouldn't you be able to control them?

06:36.403 --> 06:37.821
Whoa. Hey, hold on!

06:41.282 --> 06:42.117
Hikawa!

06:44.327 --> 06:45.161
Ah...

06:47.956 --> 06:50.417
Oh, I... I'm so sorry, Miss.

06:53.253 --> 06:55.713
No! No, no, no!

06:57.715 --> 06:59.551
Alright, calm it down, brain!

06:59.634 --> 07:01.803
Do it. Do it!

07:02.303 --> 07:05.890
SOFT BREATHING

07:05.974 --> 07:06.850
A sea slug?

07:07.642 --> 07:09.936
Oh, yeah! Mm-hm. Looking good!

07:10.019 --> 07:11.563
Mm. Look here, now here.

07:11.646 --> 07:13.064
Wow! Hm?

07:13.148 --> 07:14.441
You free the day after tomorrow?

07:14.524 --> 07:15.358
Yota?

07:19.487 --> 07:21.531
Sorry, I have practice all day.

07:21.614 --> 07:22.907
Roger that.

07:25.785 --> 07:27.579
- Yota.
- Huh?

07:28.663 --> 07:29.831
Did I keep you waiting?

07:30.832 --> 07:31.666
Not at all.

07:32.459 --> 07:34.252
You're pretty easy to spot.

07:34.961 --> 07:35.879
Well, that's good.

07:36.504 --> 07:38.423
PUFFY FLUFFY

07:38.506 --> 07:41.009
- And you're all puffy, Yota.
- You're all fluffy.

07:41.092 --> 07:42.510
Sorry to drag you with me.

07:43.011 --> 07:44.012
It's fine.

07:44.095 --> 07:46.764
I've also been wanting to see where
Miki works.

07:46.848 --> 07:48.766
I know it's hard to go alone.

07:49.684 --> 07:51.811
I marked the location here on the map.

07:52.395 --> 07:53.897
Wow! You're so prepared.

07:54.439 --> 07:55.273
Hmm.

07:56.149 --> 07:57.817
- This way.
- Why, thank you.

07:59.152 --> 08:01.070
DREAM DREAM BURGER

08:02.363 --> 08:03.281
Hi, welcome...

08:03.364 --> 08:04.782
Oh! Hey, you guys!

08:05.283 --> 08:08.286
HUFF, HUFF

08:08.369 --> 08:09.245
What happened to you?

08:09.329 --> 08:11.664
We... we wandered around for thirty
minutes.

08:12.165 --> 08:15.210
What? Why?
It's only five minutes from the station.

08:15.835 --> 08:18.129
- Hm?
- I think it's the other way, Koyun.

08:18.630 --> 08:19.631
What?

08:20.632 --> 08:23.009
Sorry for asking you to come at such a
weird time.

08:23.092 --> 08:26.179
- Thank you.
- I- I can't really talk 'til after lunch.

08:27.180 --> 08:30.642
This is the most popular one, but I
personally recommend the one with

08:30.725 --> 08:31.726
avocado.

08:32.393 --> 08:33.853
Yota, you'll like this one.

08:33.937 --> 08:34.812
It's spicy!

08:34.896 --> 08:36.272
That's what I'll get.

08:36.356 --> 08:37.315
Oh, wow!

08:37.398 --> 08:39.317
Uh, hold on a sec.

08:39.400 --> 08:41.236
Take your time, don't worry!

08:42.278 --> 08:43.571
I'll get... the avocado.

08:44.072 --> 08:46.199
Okay. Order in!

08:46.282 --> 08:47.617
A chili and an avocado!

08:47.700 --> 08:50.161
- Okay.
- Hey, Miki.

08:51.538 --> 08:53.206
Are they in a relationship?

08:53.289 --> 08:54.207
Huh?

08:54.290 --> 08:56.793
No way. They're not dating.
We're all just friends.

08:56.876 --> 08:57.961
Oh, really?

08:58.628 --> 09:02.715
I mean... they just look really
cute together, is all.

09:03.466 --> 09:06.469
- Huh?
- The short girl with the tall guy.

09:06.553 --> 09:07.387
Look at that.

09:08.012 --> 09:09.222
Aren't they a cute pair?

09:10.223 --> 09:11.808
So heartwarming, gives me the feels.

09:11.891 --> 09:13.226
Yota and Koyun.

09:14.769 --> 09:17.480
It's literally never crossed my
mind until now.

09:18.106 --> 09:20.567
But if those two started dating...

09:21.442 --> 09:22.986
What would I do?

09:25.405 --> 09:26.948
Support the heck out of them.

09:27.031 --> 09:28.866
That'd be good... really good!

09:28.950 --> 09:31.995
Koyun would be way happier if she dated
someone like Yota.

09:33.329 --> 09:34.163
Don't need one.

09:34.247 --> 09:36.291
Ugh, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no!

09:36.374 --> 09:37.709
I've learned my lesson.

09:37.792 --> 09:40.211
I shouldn't meddle in her love
life anymore.

09:40.295 --> 09:41.337
Hm?

09:44.007 --> 09:45.592
How do I eat this?

09:47.093 --> 09:49.429
There's no way this'll fit in my
mouth, right?

09:50.680 --> 09:52.765
AH LAUGH

09:54.058 --> 09:55.476
Huh? What's so funny?

09:56.603 --> 09:59.606
Yeah. This is a great idea!

10:00.189 --> 10:02.525
- AMAMIYA
- I'm home.

10:04.110 --> 10:06.154
- Welcome back.
- Oh, you're home too.

10:06.654 --> 10:08.156
What about your job?

10:08.239 --> 10:10.283
- I got off early today.
- Oh!

10:10.783 --> 10:13.453
Check out this picture of Ponta
looking like a sea slug.

10:13.536 --> 10:15.204
Wow, that's so cute!

10:16.164 --> 10:17.790
Send it to me when you get a sec.

10:17.874 --> 10:18.750
Okay.

10:19.250 --> 10:21.544
Um, let's see, where's our text thread?

10:22.629 --> 10:24.797
Huh? Yota has a profile pic now?

10:25.298 --> 10:26.466
He never does.

10:27.759 --> 10:28.843
A hamburger?

10:30.470 --> 10:31.304
Hm?

10:33.556 --> 10:34.390
Ugh!

10:37.352 --> 10:39.228
Ahh... What?

10:39.729 --> 10:41.147
Minato, you sent it yet?

10:41.856 --> 10:43.399
Uh, what're you doing?

10:43.983 --> 10:47.070
What in the world... is going on?

10:53.868 --> 10:54.827
I knew it!

10:54.911 --> 10:57.372
Yota and Hikawa are...

11:00.041 --> 11:02.085
GRADE 1 CLASS 6

11:02.168 --> 11:03.795
Winter break ended too soon.

11:04.504 --> 11:06.005
Yota, your profile pic...

11:06.506 --> 11:07.590
What's the deal?

11:08.383 --> 11:10.551
Huh? Oh, my profile?

11:11.678 --> 11:13.471
It's the same one Koyun has.

11:13.554 --> 11:14.389
CASUALLY

11:14.472 --> 11:16.140
- Miki drew it.
- Wait a sec, Miki?

11:17.809 --> 11:23.481
PRAISE ME

11:24.065 --> 11:25.608
The Alive Burger is really cute.

11:25.692 --> 11:27.443
I love all the compliments!

11:27.527 --> 11:28.486
Yeah.

11:28.569 --> 11:30.738
I learned that when Koyun and I went to
Miki's job.

11:30.822 --> 11:31.656
CRACK

11:31.739 --> 11:32.573
Just... you two?

11:33.574 --> 11:37.412
Yeah. Remember I asked if you were free,
but you said you had club activities.

11:37.495 --> 11:40.123
Ugh! Now that you mention it...

11:41.708 --> 11:44.460
The moral of the story is to be
considerate by telling people

11:44.544 --> 11:46.087
what you're inviting them to!

11:47.213 --> 11:49.257
- Yota.
- Huh?

11:50.133 --> 11:51.843
Being left out is lonely.

11:52.343 --> 11:55.096
You saying how you actually feel is very
creepy.

11:55.179 --> 11:57.724
GRADE 1 CLASS 2

11:57.807 --> 12:01.102
So, we still haven't decided who's on the
library committee.

12:01.185 --> 12:02.019
That's harsh.

12:03.646 --> 12:05.565
Winter break flew by cause I was stuck
working.

12:05.648 --> 12:08.276
The library committee eats up a
lot of after school time, doesn't it?

12:08.359 --> 12:10.319
- Yeah, I absolutely don't wanna be on it.
- But work was so slow.

12:10.403 --> 12:13.156
The shifts are flexible, the customers
are chill and also not my age, so

12:13.239 --> 12:15.074
- it's the best job I could ask for.
- I'm already a class rep.

12:15.158 --> 12:16.868
I can't take time off from my club.

12:16.951 --> 12:18.119
I hope I never lose it.

12:19.036 --> 12:22.540
Anyone not in a club and not on
a committee yet?

12:23.541 --> 12:24.375
Hm?

12:31.340 --> 12:32.175
Huh?

12:32.258 --> 12:34.051
LIBRARY COMMITTEE (2)
SHIMOJIMA, HIKAWA

12:34.135 --> 12:35.094
HIKAWA

12:35.178 --> 12:36.012
BOOM!

12:38.931 --> 12:40.558
It seems like there's a lot to do.

12:40.641 --> 12:43.644
When we're on reception duty, we
have to stay until everyone

12:43.728 --> 12:44.562
else goes home.

12:45.104 --> 12:46.481
SILENCE

12:47.273 --> 12:48.608
The silence is awkward.

12:51.152 --> 12:53.112
I have to change my work shifts.

12:54.030 --> 12:54.864
Hm?

12:55.406 --> 12:58.075
Oh, so you're not in a club either,
Shimojima?

12:58.576 --> 13:01.162
Huh? Oh, no, I'm in the art club!

13:01.746 --> 13:05.333
Uh, um, but, well, since I just kinda
draw whatever I want, people tend

13:06.042 --> 13:08.544
to think I have it easy, or how should I
put it...

13:10.129 --> 13:13.508
PISSES ME OFF, PISSES ME OFF,
PISSES ME OFF, PISSES ME OFF

13:13.591 --> 13:14.425
do nothing and have tons of free time
on our hands.

13:14.509 --> 13:17.720
All the jocks in sports clubs
think us art kids sit around and

13:17.804 --> 13:19.388
Oh no! Did I vent too much?

13:20.807 --> 13:21.808
I'm mad...

13:23.351 --> 13:26.187
At those who make assumptions and look
down on others.

13:26.687 --> 13:27.522
Huh?

13:28.189 --> 13:31.108
I didn't think that kind of stuff
happened at this school.

13:31.943 --> 13:34.028
Huh? Did she just agree?

13:35.071 --> 13:35.988
With me?

13:36.823 --> 13:37.657
Hm?

13:38.574 --> 13:39.408
Wait.

13:41.244 --> 13:42.870
- Sorry.
- Huh?

13:42.954 --> 13:44.413
I'm going that way for a bit.

13:45.122 --> 13:46.082
Yeah, sure.

13:46.666 --> 13:47.542
See ya.

13:48.876 --> 13:50.253
Oh. Okay, see ya.

13:51.504 --> 13:54.799
Hikawa really wasn't as scary as I
thought.

13:57.885 --> 13:58.719
Yota!

14:00.012 --> 14:00.847
Koyun.

14:02.807 --> 14:03.641
Ah.

14:04.517 --> 14:07.270
- Happy New Year, my friend.
- Happy New Year, my friend.

14:11.107 --> 14:12.316
What about your club?

14:13.150 --> 14:14.110
We have the day off.

14:14.193 --> 14:16.195
We can't use the gym today.

14:16.279 --> 14:17.113
Gotcha.

14:18.072 --> 14:20.074
Wait. Have you been here all this time?

14:20.157 --> 14:21.033
Yep.

14:21.534 --> 14:25.496
I like to zone out sometimes and
just look up at the sky.

14:26.372 --> 14:27.206
Oh.

14:27.915 --> 14:29.667
So, you got something on your mind?

14:30.501 --> 14:31.919
No. That's not it.

14:33.546 --> 14:35.047
I don't think about anything.

14:38.467 --> 14:39.302
I see.

14:42.597 --> 14:43.431
So peaceful.

14:44.515 --> 14:47.351
Both this location, and Yota himself.

14:49.061 --> 14:50.271
He's so relaxed.

14:51.063 --> 14:52.565
Like a passing cloud.

14:54.483 --> 14:56.819
Well, he's so tall his head's
basically in them.

14:56.903 --> 14:57.904
HEH HEH

14:59.238 --> 15:01.407
Not thinking about anything is hard.

15:03.826 --> 15:06.746
I'm always thinking about something,
usually worrying.

15:07.622 --> 15:10.207
Or getting angry over trivial things.

15:11.167 --> 15:13.169
An annoying habit of mine.

15:15.671 --> 15:17.173
I'm the total opposite of him.

15:19.592 --> 15:22.678
I can't imagine Yota letting himself
get bent out of shape.

15:22.762 --> 15:25.640
Or worrying about anything the way I do.

15:28.726 --> 15:29.644
That's nice.

15:31.270 --> 15:32.813
I wanna be more like him.

15:38.694 --> 15:42.198
- Agh.
- Yo, Amamiya, pay attention, would ya!

15:42.907 --> 15:43.783
Those two?

15:44.325 --> 15:45.159
Seriously?

15:54.377 --> 15:56.337
Well, I finished that one too.

15:57.380 --> 15:59.507
There're fewer people here than I
thought.

16:01.217 --> 16:02.093
An art book?

16:02.176 --> 16:05.554
Y-Yeah. I can learn a lot from reading it.

16:06.055 --> 16:07.974
But you're already so good at drawing.

16:08.474 --> 16:10.017
No, no, I'm not that good.

16:10.518 --> 16:12.603
Wait, what? Have you seen my drawings?

16:12.687 --> 16:13.729
Oh, yeah.

16:13.813 --> 16:18.150
When we were doing oil paintings,
I could see it from where I was sitting.

16:19.944 --> 16:22.446
- Sorry! I looked without asking.
- Swish.

16:22.530 --> 16:24.740
What? It's fine, it's fine. Come back.

16:28.285 --> 16:30.287
- See ya!
- See ya later.

16:33.457 --> 16:35.793
Maybe I should look at some art
books too.

16:36.419 --> 16:38.504
I wonder which one I should start with.

16:38.587 --> 16:40.297
GROWL

16:43.300 --> 16:44.135
Huh?

16:47.138 --> 16:48.723
He's easy to spot.

16:50.307 --> 16:52.059
CLEARLY YOTA

16:53.853 --> 16:55.730
- THUD
- Oh, sorry!

16:56.230 --> 16:57.273
Oh! Koyun.

16:57.773 --> 16:59.358
You scared me.

17:01.694 --> 17:04.905
Don't you know how dangerous it is to be
in my blind spot?

17:04.989 --> 17:06.907
You make it sound like you're a truck.

17:12.955 --> 17:14.874
What're you doin' here? Ah, same here.

17:15.541 --> 17:17.043
Are you in a hurry?

17:18.252 --> 17:19.086
Hm?

17:23.132 --> 17:24.550
It's warming my hands up.

17:26.343 --> 17:27.428
It's gonna get cold.

17:27.928 --> 17:29.388
Don't you have dinner at home?

17:29.472 --> 17:30.514
What about that?

17:31.098 --> 17:32.475
Oh no, it's fine.

17:35.019 --> 17:36.437
I can manage both just fine.

17:37.354 --> 17:38.189
Figures.

17:38.898 --> 17:42.151
I noticed you've been staying late
after school recently.

17:42.234 --> 17:44.737
Oh, I'm on library duty right now.

17:45.237 --> 17:47.490
Ah, they forced it on you?

17:48.491 --> 17:50.076
That's not what happened.

17:50.993 --> 17:53.245
Hm? Wait, is that what happened?

17:55.915 --> 17:59.919
Although I've become interested in
things I'd never been exposed to before.

18:00.002 --> 18:01.462
So it's not all that bad.

18:01.545 --> 18:02.379
Or not yet.

18:03.172 --> 18:04.632
And I have time to daydream.

18:05.174 --> 18:06.008
Oh, really?

18:06.092 --> 18:08.469
I should've picked library committee too, then.

18:09.595 --> 18:11.931
Your club activities don't leave you any
time.

18:12.640 --> 18:13.474
Hmm.

18:14.809 --> 18:17.645
But spending my time daydreaming
sounds nice.

18:20.523 --> 18:21.899
Talking with Yota...

18:22.650 --> 18:24.110
I feel so at ease.

18:26.862 --> 18:27.696
It feels warm.

18:36.080 --> 18:38.082
The fries aren't salty enough today.

18:38.165 --> 18:40.793
- Huh? Mine are really good.
- Hikawa and Yota.

18:45.047 --> 18:46.423
I wish they wouldn't.

18:49.760 --> 18:52.054
Because if you fall in love with Yota...

18:52.138 --> 18:54.014
You'll just end up getting hurt.

18:59.687 --> 19:01.272
Isn't your house that way, Yota?

19:01.355 --> 19:02.356
Yeah.

19:02.439 --> 19:04.358
But I'll walk you to the station.

19:04.441 --> 19:05.651
Oh, you don't have to.

19:06.152 --> 19:08.821
I'm just kinda worried you'll get lost.

19:08.904 --> 19:10.114
I won't get lost.

19:13.993 --> 19:14.827
Yota!

19:18.998 --> 19:20.749
Agh! That scared me.

19:20.833 --> 19:23.335
Turn on your lights. Jeez.

19:26.964 --> 19:29.258
- Are you okay?
- Y- Yeah.

19:29.842 --> 19:30.676
Sorry.

19:31.510 --> 19:32.678
Here, hold on to me.

19:33.929 --> 19:34.805
There you go.

19:47.276 --> 19:48.235
Is something wrong?

19:49.236 --> 19:50.905
Huh? Uh, no.

19:51.780 --> 19:52.615
Just now...

19:54.366 --> 19:56.327
It reminded me of when I was a kid.

19:57.536 --> 20:00.122
I-I suddenly remembered my dad.

20:01.248 --> 20:02.708
It felt floaty.

20:02.791 --> 20:06.003
- FLOATY
- Wait, what am I even saying?

20:08.422 --> 20:11.091
Then I'll let it slide if you
accidentally call me Dad.

20:11.175 --> 20:14.011
That's what elementary school kids
do to their teachers.

20:17.765 --> 20:18.849
I see now.

20:19.475 --> 20:20.601
That's why they do it.

20:22.770 --> 20:25.231
I wonder... how my dad's doing.

20:30.319 --> 20:33.656
If you were my kid, I'd have to go to the
Lost Child Center every time you left

20:33.739 --> 20:34.573
the house.

20:34.657 --> 20:37.243
I told you I wouldn't get lost
every time.

20:39.745 --> 20:40.579
Yota, hi!

20:41.288 --> 20:42.122
Huh?

20:49.797 --> 20:50.673
Why're you here?

20:51.799 --> 20:53.425
I forgot something at the store.

20:54.551 --> 20:56.095
And Haruto and Sakura?

20:57.096 --> 20:58.973
Oh, your dad's at home with them.

20:59.056 --> 21:01.392
Oh, so he got home early today.

21:01.475 --> 21:02.851
I'm assuming you already had dinner?

21:02.935 --> 21:03.769
A family member?

21:03.852 --> 21:05.854
I didn't actually. Sorry I didn't
reach out sooner.

21:05.938 --> 21:08.899
Is she his sister?
I'm wondering if maybe I should go home.

21:09.900 --> 21:12.111
- Yota.
- Well, be there soon.

21:12.194 --> 21:14.196
I- I'm walking my friend to the station.

21:14.947 --> 21:15.781
Huh?

21:16.949 --> 21:17.992
Oh, okay.

21:18.784 --> 21:19.618
Be careful.

21:32.506 --> 21:34.008
Yota, everything okay?

21:34.508 --> 21:35.634
Hm?

21:35.718 --> 21:36.552
With, um...

21:37.428 --> 21:38.262
Well...

21:38.762 --> 21:40.472
- Your sist-
- My mom.

21:41.265 --> 21:42.099
Huh?

21:43.350 --> 21:45.894
That woman is my mother.

21:46.645 --> 21:50.190
?? YEARS OLD - 16 YEARS OLD = ??

21:52.067 --> 21:53.777
Not related by blood, obviously.

21:55.279 --> 21:58.657
My real mother died when I was in
elementary school.

22:06.165 --> 22:08.625
Oh, I'm sorry. That's the normal reaction.

22:08.709 --> 22:09.835
Oh. No...

22:11.337 --> 22:13.756
It, it happened a long time ago, so I'm
fine.

22:14.923 --> 22:15.799
And well now...

22:17.009 --> 22:18.302
They're my real family.
